# Launch-from-Linux-box: do NOT upload the 34GB local data/audio via workdir.
# The dataset ships as .work/pron_audio.tar, staged deliberately by each
# sky_*.yaml's file_mounts (see `*.tar` below — the tar is excluded here so the
# workdir copy can't carry it too). Workdir upload is then just ~89MB of code.
data/audio
# g2pW's 607MB ONNX model (used only by the local scripts/audit_g2p_backends.py
# bake-off provider) — never needed on the training cluster.
G2PWModel
**/__pycache__
**/.cache
*.tar
.sky-venv
# Local scratch: Pimsleur download artifacts (8.6G), a Linux-local venv (1.1G)
# and a pip cache (239M). `*.tar` above already kept the 35G dataset tarball out
# of the workdir, which made .work look handled — it wasn't, and sky measured a
# 10.4G workdir against the ~89MB of code this file claims. None of it is usable
# on the cluster; a venv built here is actively wrong there.
# The `~/data.tar: .work/pron_audio.tar` file_mount is unaffected: file_mounts
# are staged deliberately, not filtered through .skyignore — same as `*.tar`
# has always relied on.
.work
